00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:06,100
Lighten up! Gee!

250
00:13:08,640 --> 00:13:10,820
Now, is there a doctor on board?

251
00:13:11,160 --> 00:13:12,000
I'm a doctor.

252
00:13:12,400 --> 00:13:13,740
Oh, terrific. Hi.

253
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:18,160
Listen, the woman sitting behind you, this guy's wife, she says she's going into

254
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:21,640
labor. Well, I can, uh, I can take a look at her.

255
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:23,680
Hey, Doc, don't you need a little black bag or something?

256
00:13:23,820 --> 00:13:24,800
I'm a psychiatrist.

257
00:13:24,920 --> 00:13:26,620
Oh, Doc, she don't think she's having a baby.

258
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:27,440
She's having a baby.

259
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:31,300
A psychiatrist is a medical doctor.

260
00:13:31,360 --> 00:13:34,420
Oh, hey, uh, don't tell my wife you're a head shrinker, huh?

261
00:13:35,740 --> 00:13:37,280
Hello? Hi. I'm Dr.

262
00:13:37,540 --> 00:13:39,640
Seaver. I understand you're going into labor?

263
00:13:39,900 --> 00:13:41,980
All right, well, how far apart are the contractions?

264
00:13:42,340 --> 00:13:44,400
Ooh, my, my water broke.

265
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:46,840
Would you have the captain radio head for an ambulance?

266
00:13:46,980 --> 00:13:49,140
Ambulance! Ambulance! Everything's fine.

267
00:13:49,360 --> 00:13:51,520
Everything's fine. We'll be on the ground long before the baby arrives.

268
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:52,860
Oh, okay. Hi, folks.

269
00:13:52,940 --> 00:13:54,140
This is Captain Kirk.

270
00:13:57,500 --> 00:14:01,640
Logan International is having a little fog problem, and we're gonna circle a bit.

271
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:03,300
So relax and have a drink.

272
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:05,420
Oh, no, no, no, no, no, no.

273
00:14:05,420 --> 00:14:06,520
Everything's going wrong here.

274
00:14:06,520 --> 00:14:07,380
Calm down, Cunny.

275
00:14:07,380 --> 00:14:08,680
There's no reason to panic.

276
00:14:08,780 --> 00:14:12,600
Everything's fine. Yeah, you don't see me throwing a fit, and I've got to haul out

277
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:13,960
that stupid drink cart.

278
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:14,340
I'll take a seat.

279
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:18,640
All right. There's more room up here.

280
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:19,460
You'll be more comfortable.

281
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:21,840
Why do we need more room?

282
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:23,040
What's gonna happen?

283
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:24,740
You said we'd be on the ground by now, didn't you?

284
00:14:24,740 --> 00:14:25,160
Did he say that?

285
00:14:25,160 --> 00:14:27,480
He did. Okay.

286
00:14:27,820 --> 00:14:29,100
Okay, what do we do now, huh?

287
00:14:29,100 --> 00:14:30,040
More water, ripped sheets?

288
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:33,060
What? Honey, you're scaring me.

289
00:14:33,140 --> 00:14:34,680
Yeah. You're scaring me too, Dan.

290
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:36,140
Oh, yeah. You sit over here, please.

291
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:38,960
Susan, you sit right there.

292
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:41,480
In the magic carpet lounge?

293
00:14:41,920 --> 00:14:49,740
Yeah. Dan, you know, you could be a big help if you just take a stroll, all right?

294
00:14:49,840 --> 00:14:51,200
Calm down. Yeah, that's it.

295
00:14:51,220 --> 00:14:52,820
I'll take a nice brisk walk outside.

296
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:54,060
It'll do me good.

297
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:57,140
Mike, will you watch him, please?

298
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:59,500
All right, Dad, but if he opens the door, he's on his own.

299
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:05,500
Are you comfortable, Susan?

300
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:08,200
I haven't been comfortable in five months, Doctor.

301
00:15:09,780 --> 00:15:12,420
Doctor. A word in el privete?

302
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:17,260
Yeah. No! Oh, God.

303
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:19,500
What did the captain say?

304
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:23,480
He said it would take an hour for the fog to clear in at least 45 minutes to divert

305
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:24,420
to another airport.

306
00:15:24,820 --> 00:15:27,620
Oh, damn, this baby's coming in a half an hour.

307
00:15:28,280 --> 00:15:32,200
They tell you Captain Kirk, he's either got to land this plane or he's got to beam

308
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:33,380
me up an obstetrician.

309
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:35,760
That's so cute.

310
00:15:37,020 --> 00:15:40,440
Oh! Oh! I told her she shouldn't fly.

311
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:43,300
The doctor said no, but does she listen to me?

312
00:15:43,940 --> 00:15:47,160
Apparently not. Think she'll be okay?

313
00:15:47,700 --> 00:15:49,020
Oh yeah, yeah, she'll be fine.

314
00:15:49,140 --> 00:15:51,480
My dad is a great psychiatrist.

315
00:15:53,640 --> 00:15:55,540
But now he's dealing with the other end.

316
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:58,900
What's your name?

317
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:02,140
Ah, Mike. What's my name?

318
00:16:03,020 --> 00:16:04,080
Damn, that's it!

319
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:05,540
Okay, okay, Mike.

320
00:16:05,540 --> 00:16:07,920
I'm feeling much better now.

321
00:16:08,360 --> 00:16:09,320
I'm completely calm.

322
00:16:09,720 --> 00:16:11,140
Calm? Why shouldn't you be calm?

323
00:16:11,200 --> 00:16:12,160
What's going on?

324
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:13,160
Let's go back there.

325
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:15,080
Keep pushing, Susan.

326
00:16:15,080 --> 00:16:16,960
Keep pushing. When does the pain stop?

327
00:16:17,060 --> 00:16:18,260
About 18 years.

328
00:16:19,660 --> 00:16:21,460
It's happening. It's happening.

329
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:23,080
It's happening. Dan, get a hold of yourself.

330
00:16:23,140 --> 00:16:25,360
Where? Buttercup. Sweetheart.

331
00:16:25,760 --> 00:16:27,220
Munchkin. Baby doll.

332
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:28,700
Oh, man, please.

333
00:16:28,860 --> 00:16:30,020
Get the hell out of here.

334
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:31,480
You're making me feel awful.

335
