Yeah, but I'm your coach.

336
00:16:32,980 --> 00:16:35,760
If I need a coach, You're the first one I'll call.

337
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:36,520
Now get out!

338
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:38,380
Don't take it personally, Dan.

339
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:39,640
Yeah, I know, Doc.

340
00:16:39,700 --> 00:16:41,540
I know. I took Lamont's classes, Mike.

341
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:44,740
And I know a woman tends to freak out when she reaches the final stage of labor.

342
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:46,580
The final stage of labor!

343
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:50,420
Mike! So, Dan, tell me all about those race car classes you do.

344
00:16:50,420 --> 00:16:53,580
Cars? Oh! Oh!

345
00:16:56,260 --> 00:16:57,160
Got a sec?

346
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:06,540
Doctor, I have two messages from Captain Kirk.

347
00:17:06,980 --> 00:17:10,380
First, he says he could have you on the ground in 65 seconds, but he doesn't think

348
00:17:10,380 --> 00:17:11,380
you'd enjoy the landing.

349
00:17:11,780 --> 00:17:17,080
Oh! And second, he didn't care for your Captain Kirk joke as much as I did.

350
00:17:18,980 --> 00:17:22,700
Oh! Oh! You hear that?

351
00:17:23,300 --> 00:17:24,260
I think everybody heard that.

352
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:27,140
Oh, I blew it.

353
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:28,880
That's all there is to it, I blew it.

354
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:29,780
Don't argue with me, kid.

355
00:17:30,500 --> 00:17:31,080
I'm a wimp.

356
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:32,180
Go ahead and say it.

357
00:17:33,220 --> 00:17:34,100
Okay, you're a wimp.

358
00:17:34,200 --> 00:17:34,880
Who asked you?

359
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:37,680
Wouldn't you be freaking out if your wife was having a baby?

360
00:17:38,180 --> 00:17:40,000
Heck, I'd freak out if I even had a wife.

361
00:17:41,220 --> 00:17:42,760
What kind of father am I?

362
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:44,840
Can't even watch my own kid being born.

363
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:48,100
I mean, my kid's gonna hate me.

364
00:17:49,300 --> 00:17:52,180
Ah, this whole deal of having a baby, big mistake.

365
00:17:52,680 --> 00:17:54,040
Hey, you know, I have never gotten one.

366
00:17:54,100 --> 00:17:55,220
People even have kids.

367
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:58,620
Hey, everybody knows why you have kids.

368
00:17:59,500 --> 00:18:03,800
You do it to bring somebody into the world that's part you and part your wife.

369
00:18:05,040 --> 00:18:07,220
Uh -huh. Yeah.

370
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:11,220
I mean, it's like having somebody around who can learn from your mistakes.

371
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:17,380
I mean, like, uh, say somewhere down the line, all of a sudden my kid wants to say,

372
00:18:17,380 --> 00:18:19,460
uh, move to Pittsburgh.

373
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:21,420
I say, no way I lived there.

374
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:28,700
And if he, uh, ever wants to be cool and smoke, Well, I'll tell him.

375
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:30,700
You ain't gonna do that, pal.

376
00:18:31,420 --> 00:18:32,900
It took me three years to quit.

377
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:38,460
And if you ever, ever think of quitting school, it'll be over my dead body.

378
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:40,480
You see, I done that.

379
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:41,520
And it stinks.

380
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:43,320
All right, I won't quit.

381
00:18:44,700 --> 00:18:52,440
Oh. Oh. Sorry, Mike.

382
00:18:55,380 --> 00:18:57,540
I guess I'm not myself today, huh?

383
00:18:58,620 --> 00:18:59,360
Hey, it's okay.

384
00:18:59,400 --> 00:19:01,140
I know another father who yells a little.

385
00:19:02,840 --> 00:19:06,100
Yeah, what am I gonna do with this kid when he wants to make some stupid mistake?

386
00:19:07,180 --> 00:19:08,160
I mean, what are you gonna do?

387
00:19:08,260 --> 00:19:09,260
You're gonna straighten him out.

388
00:19:09,820 --> 00:19:11,440
He'll just think I'm on his case.

389
00:19:11,780 --> 00:19:12,840
So who cares what he thinks?

390
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:13,480
He's just a kid.

391
00:19:13,500 --> 00:19:14,920
Now, who knows more, you or him?

392
00:19:16,600 --> 00:19:19,120
You're right. Yeah.

393
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:30,260
I am. Maybe you ought to have a kid.

394
00:19:36,720 --> 00:19:37,760
Will you listen to that?

395
00:19:38,340 --> 00:19:39,820
Now who'd bring a little baby on him?

396
00:19:40,980 --> 00:19:42,180
A baby! It's a baby!

397
00:19:42,360 --> 00:19:43,300
It's mine! It's our baby!

398
00:19:43,340 --> 00:19:43,780
It's our baby!

399
00:19:43,920 --> 00:19:44,600
We had a baby!

400
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:52,020
Honey. Honey. Honey.

401
00:19:52,140 --> 00:19:54,640
Honey. Honey, honey, we have a son.

402
00:19:55,340 --> 00:19:58,600
A son? Hey, Mike, a son.

403
00:19:58,980 --> 00:20:00,560
Yeah, right way to go.

404
00:20:04,060 --> 00:20:06,860
He's so... so...

405
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:10,920
young. Yeah, isn't he beautiful?

406
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:13,520
Congratulations, Pop. Yeah.

407
00:20:14,260 --> 00:20:16,020
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

408
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:25,440
My dad. You know, I gotta hand it to you, Dad.

409
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:26,900
You really know what you're doing.

410
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:30,760
Well, I think we have to give some of the credit to the mother.

411
00:20:32,720 --> 00:20:34,360
You know, you are really something.

412
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:44,480
Thank you. Dad, this college thing, um, you know, if you think this is really

413
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:46,700
important, then maybe I should at least give it a shot.

414
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:48,200
What's the catch, Mike?

415
00:20:48,380 --> 00:20:49,680
No, no, Dad, there's no catch.

416
00:20:49,680 --> 00:20:51,020
I just been thinking,

417
00:20:51,680 --> 00:20:53,420
I mean, who knows more, you or me?

418
00:20:55,360 --> 00:21:00,200
Hey, Doc, for now on, we're gonna have all our kids delivered by a psychiatrist.

419
00:21:01,640 --> 00:21:03,380
He's a psychiatrist?

420
00:21:08,940 --> 00:21:09,640
["The Star -Spangled Banner"]

421
00:21:11,230 --> 00:21:13,780
And in tonight's local news roundup, drama.

422
00:21:13,980 --> 00:21:16,980
This afternoon on what began as a routine commuter flight to Boston.

423
00:21:17,760 --> 00:21:20,160
Boston? Ben, turn that back.

